## The problem

Scale is the hardest thing to teach in science. Textbooks show each level in isolation, so learners never feel how a cell relates to a planet.

## What I built

A single explorer spanning four scales: **Microcosm** (atoms, molecules, animal / bacterial / plant cells, microbiome), **Macrocosm**, **Megacosm**, and **Earth Systems**.

The Earth Systems scale covers eight topics: atmosphere, hydrosphere, biosphere, geosphere, cryosphere, weather systems, climate & feedback, and Earth as a system. Each one ships with:

- a classroom inquiry question
- a teacher facilitation cue
- a model caveat (what the visual simplifies)
- a source link

A systems lens ties every scale to one loop: **Observe → Map → Build → Measure → Learn**. Photo Mode adds camera controls for capturing scenes.

